arm64: dts: qcom: sdm630: add CAMSS_TOP_GDSC to camss

For the sdm660-mainline 7.2.y kernel (tested on v7.2.3-sdm660, Xiaomi Redmi
Note 7 "lavender", Shenchao variant, 4 GB).

Without the TOP power domain the camss_top_ahb clock does not start
("camss_top_ahb_clk status stuck at 'off'") and the CCI cannot talk to the
sensors.

Apply after 0004.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
index 35e33e793..22ed88acd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
@@ -2110,7 +2110,8 @@ camss: camss@ca00020 {
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0xc02>,
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0xc03>;
 			power-domains = <&mmcc CAMSS_VFE0_GDSC>,
-					<&mmcc CAMSS_VFE1_GDSC>;
+					<&mmcc CAMSS_VFE1_GDSC>,
+					<&mmcc CAMSS_TOP_GDSC>;
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			ports {
